## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs’ Mercury Edit 2 is a diffusion-based code editing model for autocomplete/fill-in-the-middle (FIM) and next-edit suggestions, optimized for low-latency editor workflows.
- **Provider / access:** Inception Labs API (`v1/fim/completions`, `v1/edit/completions`, model `mercury-edit-2`). No verifiable AA/OpenRouter/models.dev benchmarked listing found in this pass.
- **Release / knowledge:** Inception Labs models documentation reviewed 2026-11-14. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed sources.
- **IDs:** `mercury-edit-2`, `inception/mercury-edit-2`, `Mercury Edit 2`.
- **Context window:** 32,000 tokens total; 8,192 max output tokens (Inception docs).
- **Modalities:** Text input; text output (code/edit completions).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** $0.25/M input, $0.025/M cached input, $0.75/M output (Inception docs/local metadata).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary diffusion-based code editing model (closed weights). Architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed. Local metadata references alignment/KTO context; not independently verified from accessible official docs in this pass.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): I reviewed Inception Labs official models documentation (including FIM and next-edit API examples/specs), OpenRouter/AA/models.dev search attempts, and local metadata/prior report. Official docs provide attributable endpoint/spec/pricing/capability information for this exact specialized model, but **no independently verifiable standardized public benchmark numerics** for this project’s general LLM comparison dimensions (Terminal-Bench/Tau/GDPval-AA/Toolathon/MCP-Atlas, GPQA/HLE/AIME/AA Intelligence Index/LCR, SWE-bench/LiveCodeBench/SciCode, multimodal benchmarks) were found. Mercury Edit 2 is a specialized FIM/next-edit code editing endpoint model rather than a general conversational/agentic coding LLM; normalizing it to the repository’s standard 1–100 LLM dimensions would be misleading/non-comparable. This file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

